            {"question":"End-of-life care is also known as:","options":["Curative care","Hospice care, comfort care, supportive care, and palliative care","Preventive care","Rehabilitation care"],"answer":"Hospice care, comfort care, supportive care, and palliative care"},
            {"question":"End-of-life care is broadly provided for patients with conditions that are:","options":["Acute and reversible","Advanced, progressive, and incurable","Mild illnesses","Temporary disabilities"],"answer":"Advanced, progressive, and incurable"},
            {"question":"End-of-life care is considered an important part of:","options":["Rehabilitation","Palliative care","Emergency medicine","Preventive medicine"],"answer":"Palliative care"},
            {"question":"According to the lecture, end-of-life care helps patients:","options":["Live forever","Die with dignity","Avoid hospitalization","Recover completely"],"answer":"Die with dignity"},
            {"question":"End-of-life care includes support for:","options":["Patients only","Families only","Patients and their families","Healthcare workers only"],"answer":"Patients and their families"},
            {"question":"The primary goal of end-of-life care is to:","options":["Increase mobility","Control pain and other symptoms","Improve laboratory values","Cure disease"],"answer":"Control pain and other symptoms"},
            {"question":"End-of-life care may include:","options":["Palliative care","Supportive care","Hospice care","All of the above"],"answer":"All of the above"},
